# Sequence diagram starter
#
# Thesis: an order is accepted synchronously, and the OrderCreated event is what
# makes the rest of the system move.
#
# Sequence diagrams are their own layout: participants are ordered left to right
# by declaration order, messages top to bottom by declaration order, and the
# layout engine and direction are ignored. Style packs still apply to the
# participants, so the semantic colors stay consistent with the other diagrams.
#
# Omitted on purpose: retries, validation branches, and the worker side of the
# queue. Add them as a scenario if the failure path is the question.

...@../styles/minimal-light

shape: sequence_diagram

user: User {class: actor}
browser: Browser {class: secondary_service}
api: API {class: primary_service}
db: Database {class: datastore}
queue: Queue {class: queue}

user -> browser: submit order
browser -> api: POST /orders
api -> api: validate request
api -> db: insert order
db -> api: order id
api -> queue: publish OrderCreated
api -> browser: 201 Created
browser -> user: show confirmation
